      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is honest to acknowledge the profound exhaustion and the weight of the void you feel right now. Accepting the lack of inherent meaning doesn't have to mean accepting absolute paralysis; it can be an opening to radical honesty about how you want to spend your remaining energy. If the struggle is pointless, then perhaps the only honest act left is to allow yourself to rest from the performance, without the pressure to *solve* anything.",
